{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And let them rejoice</b> — the sense is 'and they shall take shelter in him' — because he mentioned 'those who take shelter in you,' and the word is from the doubled-conjugation roots, and the samekh comes without dagesh, in the manner of והקל מעליך."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Resolved ותסך עלימו as Aramaic-influenced Hebrew meaning 'and they shall shelter in him'; the phrase is elliptical and the syntax is compressed in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:15.501759456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}